{
  "title": "Energy",
  "uid": "energy-kepler",
  "tags": [
    "energy",
    "kepler",
    "power"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 42,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "Mimir",
          "value": "mimir-metrics"
        },
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "node",
        "label": "Node",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(kepler_node_info, instance)",
          "refId": "node"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(kepler_node_info, instance)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Overview",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Where the numbers come from",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Measured:** CPU package and RAM from RAPL (Kepler; yojimbo's Kaby Lake has no DRAM domain, so its RAM is Kepler's estimate), the GTX 1070 from `nvidia-smi` (only while llama-cpp-cuda runs, it shares that pod's GPU claim), AMD GPUs from the amdgpu driver's PPT sensor (node-exporter hwmon).\n\n**Estimated:** per-pod power is the measured CPU/RAM power split by each container's CPU time.\n\n**Not available:** the rest of the board, disks, fans and PSU losses: no sensor reports them (Kepler's whole-board model reads ~100 W per node here, far off, so it is left out). The Disk row shows activity instead. For wall power use a smart plug."
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "id": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Measured now (CPU + RAM + GPU)",
      "description": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(sum by (instance) (rate(kepler_node_package_joules_total{instance=~\"$node\"}[$__rate_interval]))) + sum(sum by (instance) (rate(kepler_node_dram_joules_total{instance=~\"$node\"}[$__rate_interval]))) + (sum((sum by (node) (nvidia_smi_power_draw_watts{node=~\"$node\"})) or (sum by (node) (label_replace({__name__=~\"node_hwmon_power_(average|input)_watts\", instance=~\"$node\"} * on (instance, chip) group_left (chip_name) node_hwmon_chip_names{chip_name=\"amdgpu\"}, \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"(.*)\")))) or vector(0))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watt",
          "decimals": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "id": 3
    },
